Inspired by Sporkhack's changes to the starting equipment of the
wizard and rogue, here are some interesting permutations of starting
equipment for the other classes:

1. healer: two blessed eucalyptus leaves and way less gold.
The leaves act as temporary magic whistles. Instead of getting gold
(and therefore a ton of AC) for free, the healer has to rely on his
pets more carefully.

2. Archaeologist: some sort of equipment to "restore" damaged weapons
such as a guaranteed potion of oil or can of grease. Perhaps a
spellbook of "repair armor" (and "knock" for entering all those
forbidden temples) as well (Spork).
Part of a real Arc's job is to restore ancient artifacts he digs up,
so I think the ability to restore weaponry/armor from a damaged state
is appropriate. Furthermore, it would make it easier for an arc to
rely on a dwarvish mattock as his primary weapon, since those have a
propensity to rust.

3. monk: ten blessed +1 shuriken.
Shuriken are the most practical (unrestricted :)) ranged weapon for a
monk. I'm interested in how the playing style would change if shuriken
came "in the box", but in a small quantity. They're traditionally
associated with warrior monks anyway.

Then again, monks are already pretty buff in Sporkhack, so this change
might be leaning towards Munchkinization.


